# ForgeMVP - Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Rule of thumb: this file excludes what must NEVER enter the build context
# (secrets, VCS metadata, dependencies, caches, editor cruft) and nothing else.
#
# It deliberately does NOT exclude the repo's own source, tests or deployment
# files, even where they look "unnecessary" for a Linux image. The Dockerfile's
# verify stage runs the full test suite inside the build, and those suites assert
# on real repo files (start.bat, the Windows launcher, Dockerfile, cloudbuild.yaml).
# Excluding them makes `readFile` throw ENOENT and fails the build - which is what
# happened on the first attempt. tests/container.test.mjs now guards against
# reintroducing that.
#
# The shipped runtime image stays lean regardless: its stage copies only
# server.js, package.json and public/ from the verify stage.

# --- version control and CI metadata ---
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# --- dependencies and package-manager noise ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm
.pnpm-store
.yarn

# --- secrets and local environment files (never ship these) ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- build caches and generated output (this project has no build step) ---
.cache
.parcel-cache
.next
.nuxt
.turbo
.svelte-kit
dist
build
out
coverage
.nyc_output
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
.vite
.scratch

# --- editors and operating systems ---
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
